## UX / UI Design

### Layout & Hierarchy

- **One focal point per viewport.** Don't compete for attention. Guide the eye with size, contrast, and whitespace
- **Whitespace is structure.** Generous spacing signals importance and creates breathing room. Cramped layouts feel unfinished
- **Group by proximity.** Related elements closer together, unrelated elements further apart. No ambiguous gaps
- **Consistent grid.** Use the 12-column grid at desktop, collapse to 8-col at tablet, single-column on mobile
- **Progressive disclosure.** Show the minimum needed upfront; reveal detail on interaction (modals, expandable cards)

### Typography

- **Two font families max**: `Cormorant Garamond` (serif) for headings and personality, `Geist` (sans) for body and UI, `Geist Mono` for code
- **Type scale with ratios** — don't pick arbitrary sizes. Use `clamp()` for fluid scaling between breakpoints
- **Line length 45–75 characters** for readability on body text
- **Weight creates hierarchy**: bold for primary, medium for secondary, regular for body. Don't lean on size alone
- **Letter-spacing**: tighter on large headings (−0.5px), wider on small uppercase labels (0.08–0.2em)

### Color & Contrast

- **Primary blue `#001dd9`** as the single accent. Derive everything else from it
- **Minimal palette.** White background, near-black text, one accent. Restraint is sophistication
- **4.5:1 contrast minimum** for body text. 3:1 for large text (18px+)
- **Opacity for depth**: use `rgba` and opacity to create layers, not new colors
- Surface hierarchy: `--color-bg` > `--color-surface` > `--color-surface-dark`

### Interaction Design

- **Every interactive element needs three states**: default, hover, active. No exceptions
- **Hover feedback within 100ms.** Humans perceive delays above this as sluggish
- **Transitions 200–300ms** for UI state changes. Shorter feels abrupt, longer feels slow
- **Entrance animations 200–400ms.** Exit animations can be faster (150–250ms)
- **Drag interactions need visual affordance**: cursor change, shadow lift, scale shift
- **Provide undo/escape.** Every modal closes on Escape and backdrop click. Every destructive action has a way back

### Responsive & Mobile

- **Touch-first on mobile.** No hover-dependent interactions. Anything revealed on hover must be accessible another way
- **Bottom-reachable navigation** on mobile — thumbs reach the bottom of the screen, not the top
- **Simplify, don't shrink.** Mobile isn't a smaller desktop. Rethink layout, reduce cognitive load, prioritize primary actions
- **Native cursor on mobile** (< 1024px). Custom cursor is desktop-only
- **Swipe gestures** for card stacks and carousels on mobile with Framer Motion drag

